# Written before the certificates were copied in, not after.
#
# The order matters: a key that reaches a commit is a key that has to be
# reissued, and `git rm --cached` does not remove it from history. Ignoring it
# first is the only version of this that is not a race.

# TLS material. The whole directory, and then the extensions again on their
# own — a certificate that gets dropped somewhere else in a hurry is exactly
# the one nobody notices in a diff.
cert/
*.pfx
*.p12
*.key
*.pem
*.cer
*.crt

node_modules/
dist/
